<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sang Nila Utama</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">13th century</span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a> · Also known as Sri Tri Buana</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Sang Nila Utama is the legendary founder of the Kingdom of Singapura, known from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/malay-annals">Malay Annals</a>. According to the story, this prince of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/palembang">Palembang</a> landed on the island of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/temasek">Temasek</a>, saw a beast he took for a lion and named the place Singapura, the 'lion city', around 1299. His dynasty ruled until about 1400, and its last king founded <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/malacca">Malacca</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/sang-nila-utama.jpg" alt="Sang Nila Utama" width="320" height="427" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Altopian1 · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Statue_of_Sang_Nila_Utama_at_the_Raffles_Landing_Site_(three-quarter_front_view).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
